@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:f05143ad21ab9a13e727098647bde8c4d46eb68f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It now asserts what holds in any shape: the limit is respected, the newest is first, a range reaching nothing new is empty, a wider range contains a narrower one, and an unknown revision is an error." }
~ The test now asserts what holds in any shape of history.

To make the test more robust and applicable to different shapes of history, including those with merges.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:f05143ad21ab9a13e727098647bde8c4d46eb68f }, "code:kind": decline, "ingest:quote": "It asserted that HEAD~3..HEAD is three commits, which is true until a merge lands — and then the range properly contains everything the merged branch brought." }
~ The test no longer assumes history is a straight line.

To handle cases where history includes merges, which can alter the expected number of commits in a range.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "assert_eq!(all.len(), 5, \"a limit is a limit\");" }
~ The test now checks if the limit is respected.

To ensure that the function correctly handles limits on the number of commits returned.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "// Newest first: the first is HEAD itself.\nlet head = read_commit(&repo, \"HEAD\").unwrap().sha;\nassert_eq!(all[0], head);" }
~ The test now checks if the newest commit is first in the range.

To ensure that the function returns commits in the correct order, with the newest first.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "// A range reaching nothing new is empty, whatever the shape of the history.\nassert!(commits_between(&repo, Some(\"HEAD\"), \"HEAD\", 0)\n    .unwrap()\n    .is_empty());" }
~ The test now checks if a range reaching nothing new is empty.

To ensure that the function correctly handles cases where the start and end of the range are the same commit.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "// And a wider range contains a narrower one: `HEAD~1..HEAD` is part of `HEAD~3..HEAD`.\nlet near = commits_between(&repo, Some(\"HEAD~1\"), \"HEAD\", 0).unwrap();\nlet far = commits_between(&repo, Some(\"HEAD~3\"), \"HEAD\", 0).unwrap();\nassert!(!near.is_empty() && near.len() <= far.len());" }
~ The test now checks if a wider range contains a narrower one.

To ensure that the function correctly handles nested ranges, where a wider range should contain all commits of a narrower range.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "assert!(\n    commits_between(&repo, Some(\"no-such-rev\"), \"HEAD\", 0).is_err(),\n    \"an unknown revision is an error, not silence\"\n);" }
~ The test now checks if an unknown revision is an error.

To ensure that the function correctly handles invalid revisions by returning an appropriate error.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let Ok(all) = commits_between(&repo, None, \"HEAD\", 5) else {\n    eprintln!(\"history not in this clone (shallow?); skipping\");\n    return;\n};" }
~ The test now checks if the function correctly handles shallow clones.

To ensure that the function can operate in environments where the full history may not be available.

