@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "// And a wider range contains a narrower one: `HEAD~1..HEAD` is part of `HEAD~3..HEAD`.\nlet near = commits_between(&repo, Some(\"HEAD~1\"), \"HEAD\", 0).unwrap();\nlet far = commits_between(&repo, Some(\"HEAD~3\"), \"HEAD\", 0).unwrap();\nassert!(!near.is_empty() && near.len() <= far.len());" }
~ The test now checks if the function correctly handles nested ranges.

To ensure that the function can handle cases where a wider range should contain all commits of a narrower range.

@decision d/gf05143ad21ab-11 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl-git/tests/history.rs@f05143ad21ab }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "assert!(\n    commits_between(&repo, Some(\"no-such-rev\"), \"HEAD\", 0).is_err(),\n    \"an unknown revision is an error, not silence\"\n);" }
